      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why are we using the `location` qualifier here for an array but the `binding` qualifier for textures2D (e.g. in Desaturate.compute)?\n\nThese unsized buffers and textures are both global shader resources and `binding` would make sense in both situations. Granted, the way GLSL uses `location` to mean different things across varyings and global uniforms is already inconsistent but I would prefer if we were consistent in how we declare global resources.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1,
