    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cae84848_880a67ea",
        "filename": "resources/sksl/compute/ArrayAdd.compute",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 2,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-09T18:55:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Metal is special, in that there everything is a \"buffer\" but OpenGL, Vulkan, and WebGPU all have uniforms in their compute shaders. In GLSL (OpenGL and Vulkan) the `in` keyword is used only for varyings like gl_GlobalInvocationID and _resources_ are declared as one would declare any good-old SSBO or uniform.\n\nI was under the impression that we wanted to stay close to GLSL. It\u0027s OK if we want to abandon that stance but I think I\u0027d like to see a plan for how all of the language idioms we are introducing now will eventually map to platforms other than Metal, especially if we\u0027re exposing Metal-style address spaces in SkSL.",
      "parentUuid": "1c6bbb08_22afaabf",
